menu "LoRa survey"

config SURVEY_DEV_EUI
    string "DevEUI, 16 hex digits (from the network's console)"
    default ""

config SURVEY_JOIN_EUI
    string "JoinEUI (AppEUI), 16 hex digits"
    default "0000000000000000"

config SURVEY_APP_KEY
    string "AppKey, 32 hex digits"
    default ""

config SURVEY_NWK_KEY
    string "NwkKey, 32 hex digits; empty for LoRaWAN 1.0.x (Helium, or TTN set to 1.0.x)"
    default ""

config SURVEY_SUBBAND
    int "US915 sub-band (TTN and Helium in the US use 2)"
    range 1 8
    default 2

config SURVEY_TX_DBM
    int "Transmit power in dBm"
    range 2 22
    default 20
    help
        The SX1262's output. 20 dBm is a fair stand-in for a field device;
        a lower value shows how much margin a weaker radio would keep.

choice SURVEY_MODE
    prompt "What one round sends"
    default SURVEY_MODE_LADDER
    config SURVEY_MODE_LADDER
        bool "Ladder: SF7 first, then SF8, SF9, SF10 until a gateway answers (at most one downlink)"
    config SURVEY_MODE_ALL
        bool "All: one uplink at each of SF7 - SF10 (up to four downlinks; private gateway or Helium)"
endchoice

config SURVEY_EVERY_S
    int "Seconds between automatic rounds (0: only on a key press)"
    range 0 3600
    default 0
    help
        On The Things Network keep a round to a few a day per device in
        normal use: the fair use policy allows 30 s of airtime and 10
        downlinks a day.

endmenu
